{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"<CHEATSHEET_V0>"},{"role":"user","content":"Write a flows workflow that splits a chunk of input text into up to N items, processes each item independently and in parallel, tolerates individual item failures so a failed item just comes back with status 'failed' instead of failing the whole run, and then merges all the results into one summary: totalProcessed, succeeded, failed counts, aggregated output, and a summary string. The item list is not known until the split step runs, so structure it as two rounds: split, then a second flow that fans out over the discovered items with Node.all and merges."},{"role":"assistant","content":"/**
 * Port of examples/fan-out-fan-in.jsx.
 *
 * Smithers shape: split Task, then `{split && <Parallel maxConcurrency={5}>}`
 * mapping `split.items` to one Task each (`continueOnFail`,
 * `timeoutMs={120_000}`), then a merge Task over the accumulated results.
 *
 * flows shape: plan width is fixed at plan time, so fanning out over
 * something a step discovered takes two rounds (Node.all's own doc says so:
 * "end the round and carry the list in the next flow's payload"). The Split
 * flow runs the splitter and hands off; the Process flow receives the items
 * as real payload data, builds a Node.all record with one process call per
 * item, and feeds the joined record into the merge action. `continueOnFail`
 * becomes `Node.catch` per item, recovering to a failed-status result.
 *
 * Deviations:
 * - `maxConcurrency` is not expressible; Node.all declares independence and
 *   the engine owns scheduling width (GAPS.md GAP-6).
 * - `timeoutMs` per task: no equivalent (GAPS.md GAP-5).
 * - Agents (splitter, processor, merger) are STUBs (GAPS.md GAP-1).
 */
import * as NodeCrypto from "@effect/platform-node/NodeCrypto"
import { FlowEngine } from "@smthrs/engine"
import { Action, Flow, Interpreter } from "@smthrs/flow"
import { Node } from "@smthrs/plan"
import * as Effect from "effect/Effect"
import * as Layer from "effect/Layer"
import * as Schema from "effect/Schema"

const WorkItem = Schema.Struct({
  id: Schema.String,
  input: Schema.String,
  context: Schema.String
})

// zod: splitSchema
const SplitResult = Schema.Struct({
  items: Schema.Array(WorkItem),
  totalItems: Schema.Number
})

// zod: processSchema (metrics omitted: z.record optional field)
const ProcessResult = Schema.Struct({
  itemId: Schema.String,
  output: Schema.String,
  status: Schema.Literals(["success", "failed"])
})

// zod: mergeSchema
const MergeResult = Schema.Struct({
  totalProcessed: Schema.Number,
  succeeded: Schema.Number,
  failed: Schema.Number,
  aggregatedOutput: Schema.String,
  summary: Schema.String
})

class ProcessFailed extends Schema.TaggedError<ProcessFailed>()(
  "fan-out-fan-in/ProcessFailed",
  { itemId: Schema.String, message: Schema.String }
) {}

/** smithers: splitter ClaudeCodeAgent. */
export const Split = Action.make("fan-out-fan-in/split", {
  payload: {
    input: Schema.String,
    operation: Schema.String,
    maxChunks: Schema.Number
  },
  success: SplitResult
})

/** smithers: processor ClaudeCodeAgent, one Task per item. */
export const ProcessItem = Action.make("fan-out-fan-in/process", {
  payload: {
    id: Schema.String,
    input: Schema.String,
    context: Schema.String,
    operation: Schema.String
  },
  success: ProcessResult,
  error: ProcessFailed
})

/** smithers: merger ClaudeCodeAgent over ctx.outputs.process. */
export const Merge = Action.make("fan-out-fan-in/merge", {
  payload: {
    results: Schema.Record(Schema.String, ProcessResult)
  },
  success: MergeResult
})

/**
 * Round two: the item list is real payload data here, so the fan-out width is
 * known at this round's plan time. One process call per item, each protected
 * by Node.catch (smithers `continueOnFail`), joined by Node.all, merged.
 */
export const ProcessAll = Flow.make("fan-out-fan-in/process-all", {
  payload: {
    items: Schema.Array(WorkItem),
    operation: Schema.String
  },
  success: MergeResult,
  body: ({ items, operation }) =>
    Node.all(
      Object.fromEntries(
        items.map((item) => [
          item.id,
          ProcessItem.call({
            id: item.id,
            input: item.input,
            context: item.context,
            operation
          }).pipe(
            // continueOnFail: a failed item becomes a failed-status result
            // instead of failing the round.
            Node.catch({
              onFailure: () =>
                Node.succeed({
                  itemId: item.id,
                  output: "",
                  status: "failed" as const
                })
            })
          )
        ])
      )
    ).pipe(
      Node.andThen((results) => Merge.call({ results }))
    )
})

/** Round one: split, then hand the discovered list to the fan-out round. */
export const FanOutFanIn = Flow.make("fan-out-fan-in/fan-out-fan-in", {
  payload: {
    input: Schema.String,
    operation: Schema.String,
    maxChunks: Schema.Number
  },
  success: MergeResult,
  body: ({ input, maxChunks, operation }) =>
    Split.call({ input, operation, maxChunks }).pipe(
      Node.andThen((split) => ProcessAll.to({ items: split.items, operation }))
    )
})

/** STUB agent seam (GAPS.md GAP-1). */
const implementations = Layer.mergeAll(
  Split.toLayer(({ input, maxChunks }) => {
    const items = input
      .split(/\d+\.\s+/)
      .map((chunk) => chunk.trim())
      .filter((chunk) => chunk.length > 0)
      .slice(0, maxChunks)
      .map((chunk, index) => ({
        id: `item-${index + 1}`,
        input: chunk,
        context: "sentence"
      }))
    return Effect.succeed({ items, totalItems: items.length })
  }),
  ProcessItem.toLayer(({ id, input }) =>
    Effect.succeed({
      itemId: id,
      output: `processed: ${input}`,
      status: "success" as const
    })
  ),
  Merge.toLayer(({ results }) => {
    const rows = Object.values(results)
    const succeeded = rows.filter((row) => row.status === "success").length
    return Effect.succeed({
      totalProcessed: rows.length,
      succeeded,
      failed: rows.length - succeeded,
      aggregatedOutput: rows.map((row) => row.output).join("\n"),
      summary: `${succeeded}/${rows.length} items succeeded`
    })
  })
)

const FanOutLayer = Layer.mergeAll(
  implementations,
  Interpreter.layer(FanOutFanIn),
  Interpreter.layer(ProcessAll)
).pipe(
  Layer.provideMerge(Action.layerImplementations),
  Layer.provideMerge(FlowEngine.layerMemory),
  Layer.provideMerge(NodeCrypto.layer)
)

export const main: Effect.Effect<typeof MergeResult.Type> = FanOutFanIn.execute(
  {
    input:
      "Analyze the sentiment of these three sentences: 1. I love Smithers! 2. AI orchestration is hard. 3. This TUI is amazing!",
    operation: "Analyze sentiment for each item independently.",
    maxChunks: 3
  },
  { executionId: "fan-out-fan-in-1" }
).pipe(
  Effect.orDie,
  Effect.provide(FanOutLayer)
)
